WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.093
A fake prison.

00:00:01.103 --> 00:00:02.319
Real cruelty.

00:00:02.329 --> 00:00:05.319
Psychologist Philip Zimbardo
built a mock prison

00:00:05.329 --> 00:00:06.909
in a Stanford basement.

00:00:06.919 --> 00:00:08.609
Young men were split into guards and

00:00:08.619 --> 00:00:09.634
prisoners.

00:00:09.644 --> 00:00:11.368
The guards grew abusive.

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:13.138
Textbooks took the lesson:

00:00:13.148 --> 00:00:15.538
give ordinary people power,
and they'll abuse

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:16.066
it.

00:00:16.076 --> 00:00:18.240
But the recordings tell a different story.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:21.445
The famous breakdown,
a prisoner screaming?

00:00:21.458 --> 00:00:23.410
He later said he was acting, though

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.177
Zimbardo disputed that.

00:00:25.187 --> 00:00:26.802
Most of the guards have since said

00:00:26.812 --> 00:00:28.750
they were intentionally acting.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:32.148
In 2019, researcher
Thibault Le Texier went

00:00:32.158 --> 00:00:35.892
through the archives and
interviewed fifteen participants.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.501
He reported that the guards had been

00:00:37.511 --> 00:00:40.801
given precise instructions,
and a recording has

00:00:40.811 --> 00:00:43.066
the warden urging one to be tougher.

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:45.941
Zimbardo rejected the
critique, but critics say

00:00:45.951 --> 00:00:49.076
the textbook lesson
stands on shaky ground.
